Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["InfraMidpoint", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"b113cfba-670e-4478-a05b-4750a4af13b8"],

Cell["LLM generated.", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4dc78a5d-d904-4b40-a6db-765a52acdd61"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"08efc07c-7e2f-479f-9819-e594ee1fb712"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["InfraMidpoint"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraMidpoint", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["p", "TI"], ",", " ", 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8cf4a688-28c1-443b-9d9a-0ec6258462eb"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the center of the oriented segment graph from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ".",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"ccbb49f4-3d8c-469d-814a-19ec67a0ca3c"],

Cell["\<\
The graph must be finite, simple, undirected and unweighted, with valid \
vertex anchors. Unsupported arguments and properties stay unevaluated. The \
head is inert until a graph-aware reader or named sampler evaluates it.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f3463a92-19c9-4ca2-add7-521ab8272f3c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One representative is one raw vertex label, including a List-valued label. \
The complete family has distinct central vertices in graph vertex order. Its \
vertex density counts the shortest paths from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 " through each central vertex. Supported measurements are \"VertexDensity\", \
\"Cardinality\", \"CountingMeasure\", \"Subgraph\" and \"RiemannianMeasure\". \
The last measure uses the existing interior-support law. \"Graph\", \
\"EdgeDensity\", \"Length\", \"Area\" and \"Volume\" are unsupported for \
these point families."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"9fc2c96c-8415-48ef-8a75-2bc89cd32740"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The segment graph contains all shortest paths from ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ", oriented toward ",
 StyleBox["q", "TI"],
 ". A central vertex minimizes Max[d(p,v),d(v,q)] within this graph. For even \
endpoint distance this selects one middle layer; for odd distance it selects \
both middle layers. Disconnected endpoints give an empty family; equal \
anchors give one point. The \"VertexDensity\" measurement equals the segment \
\"Midpoint\" measurement. RandomInfraMidpoint samples the distinct central \
vertices uniformly, independently of their occupation densities."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"b38b1f8d-b1ac-4ca1-a1a3-1d61aa5753bd"]
}, Open  ]],

